From 5998da6d533a00472be8affc5bfd4e17c5b235e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 0xFFshell <0xffshell@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:55:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Count the buttons, the way the camera and the slot writes are
 counted

CameraWritesTest counts the files that may write the player's rotation
and HandWritesTest counts the files that may write the selected slot; the
clicks had no count, and the two hand rules are worth exactly as much as
the number of places that go around them.

ButtonWritesTest scans src/main, src/api and src/launch for everything
that can press a mouse button or swing an arm and asserts that the set of
files is exactly its allow-list - the two helpers, the inventory swap, the
idle fidget (a swing with no click behind it) and the elytra's firework -
that each allow-listed file still contains the beat it is on the list for
(Cadence.Settle in both helpers, InventorySwap#tick, the fidget's punch
packet, the firework's wait for the hand, mc.gameMode in the wrapper), and
that the fidget's file has grown no click.
MSG2
Document the door hand and the button count

The AimScatter row of HUMANLIKE.md claimed doors were aimed at a point of
their own; they were not, until this change. The camera-writes paragraph
and the test list now name both hands' guards.
---
 .../java/baritone/utils/ButtonWritesTest.java | 211 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 211 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/test/java/baritone/utils/ButtonWritesTest.java

diff --git a/src/test/java/baritone/utils/ButtonWritesTest.java b/src/test/java/baritone/utils/ButtonWritesTest.java
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..70fe471c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/test/java/baritone/utils/ButtonWritesTest.java
@@ -0,0 +1,211 @@
